QuecTool release tarball
========================

Contents:
  quectool          armv7 binary (UPX-compressed)
  quectool.yaml     default configuration
  quectool.service  systemd unit
  install.sh        on-modem installer (idempotent, safe for upgrades)
  uninstall.sh      on-modem uninstaller (--purge to wipe /usrdata/quectool)

Quick install (with adb):
  adb push <this-tarball> /tmp/quectool.tar.gz
  adb shell "cd /tmp && rm -rf q && mkdir q && cd q \
    && tar xzf ../quectool.tar.gz && sh install.sh"

The binary serves HTTPS on port 443 by default. A self-signed cert
is auto-generated on first boot at /usrdata/quectool/server.{crt,key}
covering every UP interface IP. Browsers warn the first time per
device — trust once, it sticks. To regenerate after a network
reconfiguration: rm the cert files and restart.

Or from a workstation in one shot, using deploy.sh from the repo:
  ./deploy.sh                                   # latest GitHub release
  ./deploy.sh v2.0.0                            # specific tag
  ./deploy.sh ./quectool-v2.0.0-armv7.tar.gz    # local tarball

After install, the UI is at  http://<modem-ip>:8080
Default credentials:         admin / quectool
Change password:             quectool passwd <new-password>  (paste hash into quectool.yaml)

Repo: https://github.com/snowzach/quectool
